L wrote:
> I don't really understand the gem/acid patch. Both gems and potions of
> acid are non-magical items, and yet you can make most potions from
> them? And, are players really going to throw away 2000 gold/points just
> for a chance at a sky blue potion?

	If sky blue potions are anything even vaguely useful, hell yes.

	Gems have no real value. If you really need gold (which is
moderately useful in the early game and worthless in the late game), one
correctly applied tripe ration will let you sell the same gem (it
doesn't even have to be a particularly valuable one) to a shopkeeper
repeatedly until he's out of money, and *then* use it for alchemy. (It
can even be the shopkeeper's tripe ration!)

	And points are not only utterly meaningless, gems have
negligable impact on the score anyway. My lowest-scoring ascension was
over four million points. A $2000 gem would be less than a twentieth of
a percent of that. If you actually care about score for some
inexplicable reason, you can make up the difference just by knocking
over a few more critters before you go kick in Rodney's door.

